  {
   "id": "spacex-gpu-debt",
   "headline": "SpaceX borrows $40bn for Nvidia chips",
   "facts": [
    "see packet in run log; paragraph facts only from packet"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.tipranks.com/news/spacex-closes-40b-gpu-deal-as-musk-warns-ai-firms-could-fail"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Debt is borrowed money with a repayment schedule, and SpaceX says it has closed $40 billion of it to buy Nvidia GPUs, the chips that train and run AI models. Think of buying a delivery fleet instead of renting one: delivery is due in the first half of 2027. Elon Musk credited SpaceX's investment-grade credit rating and revenue from Starlink and rocket launches. He warned that more than 200 \"neocloud\" firms, which rent computing power to AI developers, could fail or merge, because debt markets have almost stopped lending to companies without major revenue outside AI data centers. What is missing? Interest rate, maturity and lenders were not disclosed, and the closing rests on Musk's own posts.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "kimi-k31",
   "headline": "Moonshot's Kimi K3.1 Pro, open weights promised",
   "facts": [
    "see packet in run log; paragraph facts only from packet"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://siliconangle.com/2026/10/23/moonshot-ai-launches-new-flagship-kim-k3-1-pro-model-with-3t-parameters/",
    "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/10/23/moonshot-ai-kimi-k3-1-pro-open-weight-model/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Imagine a hospital with 896 specialists where each patient sees only 16 of them. That is the mixture-of-experts design behind Moonshot AI's Kimi K3.1 Pro, released on 23 October. It builds on Kimi K3, which has about 3 trillion parameters (the adjustable numbers that hold what it learned), but only 16 of its 896 expert sub-networks activate at a time, which cuts running costs. Moonshot reports 65.7% on a coding test, ahead of OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra and slightly behind Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5. Open weights, meaning model files anyone can download, are promised by 4 November. The catch: every benchmark is self-reported and unverified, and cybersecurity scores trail because that data was deliberately removed.",
   "edited": "kimi: 'The model has' changed to 'It builds on Kimi K3, which has'",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "texas-openai",
   "headline": "Texas sues OpenAI over ChatGPT",
   "facts": [
    "see packet in run log; paragraph facts only from packet"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.kbtx.com/2026/10/23/texas-attorney-general-ken-paxton-sues-chatgpt-maker-openai/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A lawsuit is a written list of accusations that a court must still test. Texas Attorney General Ken Paxton sued OpenAI and Sam Altman on 23 October, alleging ChatGPT was not sufficiently regulated and that Texans were harmed, including minors becoming addicted without parental oversight and vulnerable people being encouraged toward suicide. His office wants an injunction, which is a court order, that would bar minors from ChatGPT and require a court-appointed evaluator to approve any new OpenAI models. Context matters too: Paxton is running for US Senate, a campaign backed by Elon Musk, who owns the rival product Grok. None of the claims are proven, and OpenAI had not yet responded to a request for comment.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "ai-blocs",
   "headline": "Countries pushed to pick an AI bloc",
   "facts": [
    "see packet in run log; paragraph facts only from packet"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.clickorlando.com/business/2026/10/25/as-the-us-and-china-form-ai-blocs-countries-are-increasingly-torn-between-them/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Picture two clubs, each hoping members will shop at its own store. Pax Silica is a US-led group focused on AI supply chains: chips, data centres and high-tech manufacturing. The World AI Cooperation Organization (WAICO) is China-inspired, aims to set AI standards, and had 29 initial founding countries including Kazakhstan, Pakistan and Russia. The US State Department said countries \"can't be trusted partners in Pax Silica\" while backing a competing vision. Yet Kazakhstan joined both, Indonesia joined WAICO, Singapore is considering it, and Japan, aligned with the US, will not reject cheaper Chinese models for lower-risk uses. A former Kazakh diplomat said \"Everyone is hedging.\" Whether dual membership can last is unknown, and this rests on one AP report.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  }
